# Copy to .env.docker and replace every placeholder before you start the stack.
# .env.docker is gitignored. Do not commit it, and do not reuse these placeholders.
#
#   cp .env.docker.example .env.docker
#   docker compose --env-file .env.docker -f docker-compose.yml up --build
#
# Generate secrets with openssl rand -hex 32.
# Use the hex output as-is. A password with @, :, /, or # breaks DATABASE_URL.
# GARAGE_RPC_SECRET must be 64 hex characters, which is what openssl rand -hex 32 prints.
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET must be at least 32 characters.
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID and S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY are the Garage key pair. They are not AWS keys.
#
# BROWSER_API_URL is the origin the browser uses to call the API. It is read when the
# web server renders a page. Change it without rebuilding the image. It must be the
# host and port you publish for the API (API_PORT below). INTERNAL_API_URL is set by
# docker-compose.yml to http://api:3001 and is not listed here.
# WEB_ORIGIN, API_PUBLIC_ORIGIN, and PUBLIC_BASE_URL are the origins the API writes
# into links and cookies. On this published stack they match the host ports.
# Set PUBLIC_BASE_URL yourself when you change the web origin or WEB_PORT.
# An empty PUBLIC_BASE_URL becomes http://localhost:3000 in docker-compose.yml.
# It does not copy WEB_ORIGIN. The API uses WEB_ORIGIN only when the variable is
# unset, which is the from-source process.

POSTGRES_PASSWORD=replace-with-openssl-rand-hex-32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-at-least-32-characters
GARAGE_RPC_SECRET=replace-with-64-hex-characters-from-openssl-rand-hex-32
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=replace-with-an-access-key
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=replace-with-openssl-rand-hex-32
S3_BUCKET=factrove
S3_REGION=us-east-1

WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
API_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3001
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
BROWSER_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
# Optional. Source code link in the web app. Unset uses the Factrove repository.
# Set this to your fork when you run a modified version.
# SOURCE_CODE_URL=https://github.com/magnificode-ltd/factrove

WEB_PORT=3000
API_PORT=3001

# Optional. Leave unset on localhost. Hex, at least 32 characters, if you set it.
# SHARE_TOKEN_KEY=
# AUTH_COOKIE_DOMAIN=
# TRUSTED_PROXIES=

# Invite email. log writes the message and does not send it. smtp uses any SMTP server.
# brevo posts to the Brevo HTTP API. The from name defaults to Factrove.
# Leave EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS unset with log. The log then uses no-reply@localhost.
# smtp and brevo require an address. That address is the support contact.
# The footer link is WEB_ORIGIN. Factrove Cloud uses support@factrove.app.
# Do not commit BREVO_API_KEY, SMTP_USER, or SMTP_PASSWORD. The API never logs those values.
EMAIL_TRANSPORT=log
# redacted (default) hides link queries in the log. full is refused when NODE_ENV is production.
# EMAIL_LOG_LINKS=redacted
# EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=library@example.com
EMAIL_FROM_NAME=Factrove
# Optional absolute http(s) logo. Unset uses the text wordmark.
# EMAIL_LOGO_URL=
# Generic SMTP, used when EMAIL_TRANSPORT=smtp. Leave USER and PASSWORD empty together
# when the server has no AUTH. SMTP_SECURE=false is STARTTLS on port 587.
# Leave SMTP_REQUIRE_TLS unset so that connection must upgrade. false allows plaintext
# and exposes the password and the message on the network.
# SMTP_HOST=mail.example.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURE=false
# SMTP_REQUIRE_TLS=
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
# Brevo SMTP relay. The SMTP login and SMTP key are not BREVO_API_KEY.
# EMAIL_TRANSPORT=smtp
# SMTP_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURE=false
# SMTP_USER=your-brevo-smtp-login
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
# Brevo HTTP API, used only when EMAIL_TRANSPORT=brevo.
# BREVO_API_KEY=
